    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** (82.87) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) acting as the clear offensive anchors. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Lowder (4.82 xERA), whose profile suggests a prime opportunity for extra-base damage. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** finds himself in the most advantageous spot of the day; he draws a significant 19% SP skill boost from Ober\u2019s high xERA and an additional 14% cushion thanks to a favorable platoon split. **Heliot Ramos** (66.28) also warrants attention; while his base metrics are modest, his speed profile and Ober\u2019s slow delivery create a high-probability environment for stolen bases, a vital component for our 5x5 Roto standing where speed is the scarcest commodity.\n\nThe bench decision process was dictated by the strict \"Zebras Floor\" of 40.0. The most difficult exclusion was **Miguel Vargas** (52.49). Despite a strong xwOBA of 0.379 and a helpful platoon boost, his efficiency metrics failed to clear the threshold required to displace the high-scoring utility slots held by **Josh Jung** (57.91) or **Jackson Merrill** (59.77). Elsewhere, we are exercising extreme caution with **Gunnar Henderson** (50.27). While he is a perennial star, a harsh 15% penalty due to the platoon disadvantage against Manaea (L) significantly depresses his ceiling. We are keeping **Gunnar Henderson** in the lineup solely due to his talent floor, but he remains a high-risk asset today compared to the more favorable matchups enjoyed by **Coby Mayo** (53.36). \n\nRisk mitigation is paramount as we monitor the late-season game caps. **Drake Baldwin** (52.11) is active in the leadoff spot, but we must acknowledge his poor BvP history against Gausman, which carries a 7% penalty to his projection. **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined, leaving a void in our outfield speed; we continue to rely on the base-running aggression of **Heliot Ramos** and **Jackson Merrill** to offset this production gap. Barring any late-afternoon weather shifts in our park venues, this lineup is optimized to maximize run production while strictly adhering to the efficiency scores needed to protect our remaining games.",
